    "colWords": "Words",
    "colLines": "Lines",
    "colTopic": "Focus",
    "colTotal": "Total",
    "ratioNote": "one word of input per {{ratio}} lines of code",
    "readingTitle": "How to read the charts",
    "reading": "The two charts deliberately use separate axes: words and lines of code differ by more than a factor of twenty, so in a shared chart the input would be a flat line at zero. Note 15 July: two inputs, no new code – that day was documentation only. And 24 June shows that most of the program came out of a single session. Word count says little about quality: what mattered was stating the engineering requirements precisely and checking the results against building physics.",
    "s1": "Initial implementation, calculation core, 7 tabs",
    "s2": "Documentation, no new code",
    "s3": "Rebuild to tab layout, HVAC per GEG, isometric view",
    "s4": "Real map graphics, global climate zones",
    "s5": "Publication, shareable links, info tab",
    "originTitle": "Origin",
    "origin": "The model is CASAnova, developed at the Building Physics & Solar Energy department of the University of Siegen. HUUSanova is an independent reimplementation as a web application and is not affiliated with the original authors.",
